  "snippets": [
    {
      "snippet_id": "SNP-001",
      "snippet_text": "\"Etsy advertises that it takes around 3.5% commission on sales, which is of course very low. Unfortunately, that is simply not true. If you tot up all the additional fees the actual figure is closer to 15%. And that's before you've paid for postage, any marketing fees and local taxes.\"",
      "context_before": null,
      "context_after": null,
      "location_pointer": {
        "pointer_type": "url",
        "pointer_value": "https://www.thecluttery.com/blog/2025/7/29/why-i-left-etsy"
      },
      "source_finding_id": "F-08",
      "finding_part": 1
    },
    {
      "snippet_id": "SNP-002",
      "snippet_text": "\"paying for off-site ads and to appear higher in listings are both necessary to be successful on Etsy. I did pay for marketing for a year as an experiment, and I found that although I made more sales, they basically covered my marketing budget.\"",
      "context_before": null,
      "context_after": null,
      "location_pointer": {
        "pointer_type": "url",
        "pointer_value": "https://www.thecluttery.com/blog/2025/7/29/why-i-left-etsy"
      },
      "source_finding_id": "F-09",
      "finding_part": 1
    },
    {
      "snippet_id": "SNP-003",
      "snippet_text": "\"in 2025 when the USA increased their import tariffs I was effectively no longer able to sell to the USA either since customers aren't likely to buy if the postage and taxes cost more than the item itself.\"",
      "context_before": null,
      "context_after": null,
